{"title":"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the sequence of numbers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e89f1d752780c25052311294b06148c526a2fb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,7,1,8,9,7,6,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-th term of the sequence is the units digit of the sum of the two previous terms. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> denote the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms of this sequence. The smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18e57efd4af6c0e358554e7396258d85538143d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n&gt;10,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc490de10aaecf1ee23e0cba96e50f6acc92f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }1992 \\qquad \\text{(B) }1999 \\qquad \\text{(C) }2001 \\qquad \\text{(D) }2002 \\qquad \\text{(E) }2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequence is infinite. As there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of digits, sooner or later a pair of consecutive digits will occur for the second time. As each next digit only depends on the previous two, from this point on the sequence will be periodic.\n</p><p>(Additionally, as every two consecutive digits uniquely determine the <i>previous</i> one as well, the first pair of digits that will occur twice must be the first pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129cf570584aaf0e62c4213d318563c196e866d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" />.)\n</p><p>Hence it is a good idea to find the period. Writing down more terms of the sequence, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/1049243c926e198e5a723b9ad4f30bbbe056255a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4,7,1,8,9,7,6,3,9,2,1,3,4,7,\\dots\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>and we found the period. The length of the period is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and its sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414ec8814d5ca6aa2ab3418ac575e1cf751d56af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+7+\\cdots+1+3 = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"14\" />. Hence for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23dd4a4a61d38fef057984d5b03e7474bc39607f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{12k} = 60k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c8b5c5176d571b78c8adeb6ab60b39f97a6b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 10000/60 \\rfloor = 166$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d6b304f870f4923b256dc0681308c8c062103c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$166\\cdot 12 = 1992$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2fe3f0686b8ab13b20c67a2ab0742c1f6384af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1992} = 60\\cdot 166 = 9960$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" />.\nThe rest can now be computed by hand, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e49884c954044d2efbd97af4d9a3b37732eb04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1998} = 9960+4+7+1+8+9+7= 9996$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"346\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e22cf565622848e807056e5619f5d7dc63ce830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{1999}=9996 + 6 = 10002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"199\" height=\"15\" />, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/3493109a9b82ece3a1ccb02c3f4426bfda6c5e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) }1999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4T8ukzLsjx8\">https://youtu.be/4T8ukzLsjx8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A\">2002 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php